  "notes": "Cash basis. Governmental figures roll fund balance (892,812 -> 908,586, p4); no beginning governmental cash printed. ending_cash = cash and cash equivalents + cash with county treasurer (p3); certificates of deposit in ending_investments (as FY2023). Governmental statement lists spending by object only; functions taken from the dominant fund column (Other: CRA Fund dominant). Interest income printed under Other Financing Sources (Uses) goes to other_financing (as FY2024). Business-type (Water, Sewer, Solid Waste) rolls cash-basis net position (p6, same figures as the Statement of Activities p2); proprietary cash flows printed p7-8 but proprietary left null as in FY2023/FY2024. Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds statement (p3, totals equal the government-wide Governmental column), business-type from p1 Proprietary column; Elwood Care Center component unit excluded throughout (budget schedule p9 Nursing Home lines skipped). Detail: General Fund from the departmental combining statement (p10); the p9 all-funds budget schedule contributes only the Street, CRA, Water, Sewer and Solid Waste spending lines (its revenue lines are not by fund). Cemetery department = Public health and social services 1,707 on p9. Many 1-dollar rounding differences (report_discrepancies). Read pages 1-10 of 10"
